sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 56/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Judged against Klüver's families as drawn in Bressloff et al. (2001) Fig. 1 / Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): the tunnel panel is a convincing set of concentric rings, the cobweb panel is a plausible radial-plus-concentric web, and the honeycomb panel is a plausible log-polar spot lattice; the four panels are visually distinct from each other. Deductions: the \"Spiral / Funnel\" panel is a mirror-symmetric pair of nested loops rather than a recognisable spiral, and the funnel (radial rays, `rays` pattern) is never rendered although it is half of Klüver's first family (-14); no subject drawing or paper figure is placed side by side, so the match is by description only (-8); the rendered lattices are imposed by the preset `pattern`, while the model's own cubic selection for every gallery preset is hexagonal (roll_stable = False), so three of the four \"specimens\" are not what the model produces (-12); contour orientation, which distinguishes the contoured cobweb/honeycomb of Figs 31-36 from non-contoured blobs, is not shown (-6); the GIF subtitle mislabels the spiral preset as 60 degree stripes when it is rendered at 45 degrees (-4). Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): Row 2: rings convincing, cobweb and hex plausible, spiral panel reads as mirrored nested loops; no funnel/rays panel — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 9b18c52, image/png, 1048700 B, 2029×2087 px, artifact_sha256 b1c581d309d1ca62f759f511d26db59cb769c50d4aa1615f14631ebca9a943d4 (sha256 b1c581d309d1ca62f759f511d26db59cb769c50d4aa1615f14631ebca9a943d4), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): Frame 1 tunnel/rings; same four presets, non-contoured — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 9b18c52, image/gif, 2282654 B, 640×340 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 12087533329905e1581829715b978712ba3293d1dc6daea2b2e6d70615b13b11 (sha256 12087533329905e1581829715b978712ba3293d1dc6daea2b2e6d70615b13b11), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1092–L1097: Gallery of four presets; `rays` (funnel) pattern defined at line 766 but never rendered <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1092-L1097>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): kluver_form_constant rows: selected_family=roll/hexagonal, global=hexagonal, roll_stable=False while rendered=rings/spiral/cobweb — bressloff_v1_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 9b18c52, text/csv, 2983 B, artifact_sha256 525b9a2413dbd8214a47a3080df7ba044052ba336d68d52951443ebd03f2d8fa (sha256 525b9a2413dbd8214a47a3080df7ba044052ba336d68d52951443ebd03f2d8fa), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.56"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphological realism / specimen match' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

